# Copy to .env and fill in. build-app.sh sources .env automatically; .env is
# gitignored. This file documents the keys it understands.

# Code-signing identity (the Common Name of a code-signing cert in your login
# keychain). build-app.sh signs the app with this.
#
# Two things depend on it:
#   1. Keychain ACL stability — a stable cert keeps the app's cdhash constant
#      across rebuilds, so the ACL on the ClaudeUsage-credentials item stays
#      sticky and you aren't re-prompted (or forced to reconnect) each build.
#   2. The Login Items name — macOS labels the "Allow in the Background" entry
#      (System Settings → General → Login Items) by the cert's Common Name,
#      NOT by CFBundleDisplayName. Name the cert "Claude Usage" and the entry
#      reads "Claude Usage"; sign with a personal Apple dev cert and it shows
#      your name instead.
#
# Create one once via Keychain Access → Certificate Assistant → Create a
# Certificate (Self Signed Root + Code Signing, long validity). See README.md.
#
# If unset, build-app.sh falls back to "ClaudeUsage Self-Signed".
SIGN_IDENTITY="Claude Usage"
